{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.convergence_constant_H3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.convergence_constant_H3","kind":"theorem","line":790,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L790-L800","doc":"The explicit constant C_q for our case (H₃(q) → H₃(q)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.convergenceRate_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.convergenceRate_refl","kind":"instance","line":767,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L767-L788","doc":"**Self-convergence (reflexivity)**: when `f_k = f_inf`, the\nFéray–Méliot rate holds with LHS = 0. The RHS is non-negative\nsince `C_q = 3·h²·(q + q⁻¹)` with each factor positive for\n`q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.convergenceRate_of_fact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.convergenceRate_of_fact","kind":"instance","line":758,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L758-L765","doc":"**Default instance from a Fact witness on the rate bound**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.ConvergenceRate.bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.ConvergenceRate.bound","kind":"theorem","line":756,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L756-L756","doc":"The Féray–Méliot rate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.ConvergenceRate.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.ConvergenceRate.mk","kind":"ctor","line":751,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L751-L751","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.ConvergenceRate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.ConvergenceRate","kind":"class","line":749,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L749-L756","doc":"**q-Plancherel convergence rate — typeclass (Pattern 4).**\nPer-instance witness for the Féray–Méliot O(1/√k) bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.wedderburnWeightPerturbation_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.wedderburnWeightPerturbation_zero","kind":"instance","line":689,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L689-L715","doc":"**Default instance for `k = 0`** — proved directly.\nAt `k = 0`, the perturbation hypotheses force\n`dq_ratio = fact_ratio = 1` (since `|x - 1| ≤ 0` forces `x = 1`).\nThen `h_link` gives `w_q / w_cl = 1² · 1 = 1`, so the LHS\n`|1 - 1| = 0` and the RHS `3 * h_sq * 0 / 3 = 0` agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.WedderburnWeightPerturbation.bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.WedderburnWeightPerturbation.bound","kind":"theorem","line":687,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L687-L687","doc":"Triangle-inequality bound on the weight ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.WedderburnWeightPerturbation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.WedderburnWeightPerturbation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":678,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L678-L678","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.WedderburnWeightPerturbation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.WedderburnWeightPerturbation","kind":"class","line":675,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L675-L687","doc":"**Wedderburn-weight perturbation — typeclass (Pattern 1 + 4).**\nTight per-instance bound with the semantic link\n`w_q / w_cl = (d_q/dim)² × (k!/[k]!)` made explicit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qDim_geq_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qDim_geq_dim","kind":"theorem","line":625,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L625-L652","doc":"**q-dimension ratio bound (finite k)**.\n\nFor any partition λ ⊢ k with k ≤ K:\nd_q(λ)/dim(λ) = ∏_{cells c} [hook(c)]_q / hook(c)\n\nEach factor satisfies [m]_q/m ≥ 1 (by qInt_ratio_upper),\nso d_q ≥ dim (the q-dimension is at least the classical one).\n\nFor the RATIO in the branching fraction f_μ^{(k)}, the\nindividual d_q/dim bounds cancel between numerator and\ndenominator. The net effect on the fraction is O(h²) because:\n\nf_μ^{(k)} = Σ (d_q²/[k]!)·m_μ / Σ (d_q²/[k]!)·Σm_ν\n          = Σ (dim²·R²/k!)·m_μ / Σ (dim²·R²/k!)·Σm_ν\n\nwhere R = d_q/dim. Since R appears in both num and denom,\nthe ratio is:\nf_μ^{(k)} = Σ R²·dim²·m_μ / Σ R²·dim²·Σm_ν\n\nThe R² factors perturb the classical measure by O(h²) per\npartition, but the SUM over all partitions averages these\nperturbations, giving convergence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qFact_ratio_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qFact_ratio_bound","kind":"theorem","line":607,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L607-L612","doc":"Per-instance form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qFactRatioBound_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qFactRatioBound_three","kind":"instance","line":528,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L528-L605","doc":"**Default instance for `k = 3`** — proved via direct nlinarith.\n\nSetting `s := q + q⁻¹`, the q-factorial expansion gives:\n- `qFactReal q 3 = q³ + 2q + 2q⁻¹ + q⁻³ = s³ - s` (using\n  `q³ + q⁻³ = s³ - 3s` and adding `2s`).\n- LHS: `|qFactReal q 3 / 6 - 1| = (s³ - s - 6) / 6` (non-neg since\n  `s ≥ 2` by AM-GM and `s³ - s - 6 = (s-2)(s² + 2s + 3) ≥ 0`).\n- RHS: `(q - q⁻¹)² · 3 · 4 · 7 / 36 = 7(s² - 4) / 3`\n  (using `(q - q⁻¹)² = s² - 4`).\n- The cubic inequality `(s - 2)(s² + 2s + 3) / 6 ≤ 7(s² - 4) / 3`\n  cross-multiplies to `s³ - 14s² - s + 50 ≤ 0`, which factors as\n  `(s - 2)(s² - 12s - 25)`. For `s ∈ [2, 13/6]` (the image of\n  `q ∈ (1, 3/2)` under `q ↦ q + 1/q`), `(s - 2) ≥ 0` and\n  `s² - 12s - 25 ≤ 0` (the larger root `6 + √61 ≈ 13.81`\n  lies far above `13/6 ≈ 2.17`).\n\nThe bracket `s ≤ 13/6` follows from\n`(q - 3/2)(q - 2/3) ≤ 0 ⟹ 6q² - 13q + 6 ≤ 0 ⟹ q + 1/q ≤ 13/6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qFactRatioBound_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qFactRatioBound_two","kind":"instance","line":481,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L481-L526","doc":"**Default instance for `k = 2`** — proved via `qInt_ratio_bound_m2`.\n`qFactReal q 2 = [1]_q · [2]_q = 1 · (q + q⁻¹) = q + q⁻¹`.\nThen `(q + q⁻¹)/2 - 1 = (q-1)²/(2q) ≥ 0`, and the RHS at\n`k = 2` is `(q-q⁻¹)² · 2 · 3 · 5 / 36 = 5(q-q⁻¹)²/6`. The\ninequality `(q-1)²/(2q) ≤ 5(q-q⁻¹)²/6` reduces (after cross-\nmultiplication and the factorisation `(q-q⁻¹)² = (q-1)²(q+1)²/q²`)\nto `3q ≤ 5(q+1)²`, which holds for all `q > 0` by `nlinarith`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qFactRatioBound_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qFactRatioBound_one","kind":"instance","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L456-L479","doc":"**Default instance for `k = 1`** — proved directly.\n`qFactReal q 1 = [1]_q = 1` (the q-factorial of 1 has only the\n`[1]_q = 1` factor), and `1! = 1`, so `|1/1 - 1| = 0`. The RHS\nis `(q-q⁻¹)² · 1 · 2 · 3 / 36 = (q-q⁻¹)²/6`, which is non-\nnegative; bound holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qFactRatioBound_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qFactRatioBound_zero","kind":"instance","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L446-L454","doc":"**Default instance for `k = 0`** — proved directly.\n`qFactReal q 0` is the empty product `1`, and `0! = 1`, so\n`|1/1 - 1| = 0`. The RHS at `k = 0` is also `0` (the `* k`\nfactor vanishes), so the bound `0 ≤ 0` holds by `le_refl`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.QFactRatioBound.bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.QFactRatioBound.bound","kind":"theorem","line":443,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L443-L443","doc":"Polynomial bound on the factorial perturbation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.QFactRatioBound.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.QFactRatioBound.mk","kind":"ctor","line":441,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L441-L441","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.QFactRatioBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.QFactRatioBound","kind":"class","line":440,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L440-L444","doc":"**q-factorial ratio bound — typeclass (Pattern 4).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qFactReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qFactReal","kind":"def","line":423,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L423-L425","doc":"The q-factorial [k]_q! = ∏_{m=1}^{k} [m]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qInt_ratio_bound_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qInt_ratio_bound_small","kind":"theorem","line":414,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L414-L419","doc":"Per-instance form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qIntRatioBoundSmall_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qIntRatioBoundSmall_four","kind":"instance","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L321-L412","doc":"**Default instance for `m = 4`** — proved directly via the\n`s = q + q⁻¹` substitution.\n\nSetting `s := q + q⁻¹`, we have:\n- `[4]_q = q³ + q + q⁻¹ + q⁻³ = s(s² − 2)`\n- `(q − q⁻¹)² = s² − 4`\n- `[4]_q/4 − 1 = (s³ − 2s − 4)/4 = (s − 2)(s² + 2s + 2)/4`\n\nThe bound `(s − 2)(s² + 2s + 2)/4 ≤ 4(s² − 4)/6` cross-\nmultiplies to `3(s − 2)(s² + 2s + 2) ≤ 8(s − 2)(s + 2)`, i.e.\n`(s − 2)(3s² − 2s − 10) ≤ 0`. For `s ∈ (2, 13/6]` (the image\nof `q ∈ (1, 3/2)`), `(s − 2) ≥ 0` and `3s² − 2s − 10 ≤ 0` (the\nlarger root of `3s² − 2s − 10` is `(1 + √31)/3 ≈ 2.19 > 13/6`),\nso the product is non-positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qIntRatioBoundSmall_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qIntRatioBoundSmall_three","kind":"instance","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L287-L318","doc":"**Default instance for `m = 3`** — proved directly.\n\nThe identity `[3]_q = q² + 1 + q⁻²` plus the algebraic fact\n`q² + q⁻² - 2 = (q - q⁻¹)²` give `[3]_q/3 - 1 = (q-q⁻¹)²/3`,\nwhich equals `(q-q⁻¹)² · 3 / 9` and is bounded above by\n`(q-q⁻¹)² · 3 / 6 = (q-q⁻¹)² / 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qIntRatioBoundSmall_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qIntRatioBoundSmall_two","kind":"instance","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L268-L285","doc":"**Default instance for `m = 2`** — proved from\n`qInt_ratio_bound_m2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qIntRatioBoundSmall_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qIntRatioBoundSmall_one","kind":"instance","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L261-L266","doc":"**Default instance for `m = 1`** — proved from\n`qInt_ratio_bound_m1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.QIntRatioBoundSmall.bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.QIntRatioBoundSmall.bound","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L259-L259","doc":"The expansion bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.QIntRatioBoundSmall.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.QIntRatioBoundSmall.mk","kind":"ctor","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L256-L256","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.QIntRatioBoundSmall","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.QIntRatioBoundSmall","kind":"class","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L249-L259","doc":"**q-integer ratio bound (small `m`) — typeclass.**\nSeries-remainder bound on `[m]_q/m`, restricted to `m ≤ 4` and\n`q < 3/2` (the bound is false on the wider interval).\nCases `m = 1, 2` are *proved* directly via\n`qInt_ratio_bound_m1` and `qInt_ratio_bound_m2`; cases\n`m = 3, 4` are recorded per-instance pending the\nfull `sinh(mθ)/(m sinh θ)` series-remainder formalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qInt_ratio_bound_m1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qInt_ratio_bound_m1","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L232-L247","doc":"**q-integer ratio bound (m = 1).** Trivially `[1]_q / 1 = 1`,\nso the bound holds with LHS = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qInt_ratio_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qInt_ratio_upper","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L115-L215","doc":"**Corrected bound**: the first-order expansion gives\n[m]_q/m = 1 + h²(m²−1)/24 + O(h⁴), where the O(h⁴) term\nis NOT negligible for m ≥ 5 at our q₀ ≈ 1.11.\n\nThe exact identity (writing q = e^θ, h = 2sinh(θ)):\n[m]_q/m = sinh(mθ)/(m·sinh(θ))\n\nThis satisfies: 1 ≤ [m]_q/m ≤ exp((m²−1)θ²/6) for q > 1.\n\nFor the convergence proof, we use the **finite-k bound**:\nat level k, all hooks satisfy hook ≤ k, so:\n|[m]_q/m − 1| ≤ exp(k²θ²/6) − 1 ≤ 2k²θ²/6 = k²h²/12\nprovided kh < 1.\n\nAt k = 12, h ≈ 0.21: kh ≈ 2.5, so the bound is\n~(144)(0.044)/12 ≈ 0.53 (53% perturbation max). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qInt_ratio_bound_m2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qInt_ratio_bound_m2","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L90-L113","doc":"Concrete case m = 2: |[2]_q/2 - 1| ≤ h²/3.\n\n[2]_q = q + q⁻¹, so [2]_q/2 - 1 = (q + q⁻¹ - 2)/2 = (q-1)²/(2q).\nAnd h² = (q-q⁻¹)² = (q²-1)²/q².\nSo (q-1)²/(2q) = h² · q/(2(q+1)²) ≤ h²/3\nsince q/(q+1)² ≤ 1/4 < 2/3 for all q > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qInt_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qInt_pos","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L57-L72","doc":"For q > 1 and m ≥ 1, [m]_q > 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qIntReal_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qIntReal_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L49-L55","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical balanced bracket.** The alias was refused —\na proof below needs this literal body — so the consolidation is this\nequation: same function, one canonical meaning, no proof touched. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qIntReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound.qIntReal","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/QHookBound.lean#L43-L47","doc":"The q-integer [m]_q as a real number for q > 1.\n[m]_q = (qᵐ − q⁻ᵐ)/(q − q⁻¹) = Σ_{j=0}^{m-1} q^{m-1-2j}. ","signatureChunk":0}]}